\end{aligned}

Hence, $\mathrm{V}_1 \lt  \mathrm{V}_2 \lt  \mathrm{V}_3 \lt  \mathrm{V}_4$

The process in which heat remains constant is called adiabatic process.
In adiabatic process relation between temperature and volume is given as:

\mathrm{TV}^{\gamma-1}=\text { constant }

